&lt;p style="line-height: 1.7; margin: 1em 0;"&gt;No country bans Methylparaben or Ethylparaben. The US FDA does not set a specific concentration limit for any paraben — it considers parabens safe as currently used in cosmetics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style="margin-top: 1.5em; margin-bottom: 0.5em; font-size: 1.2em; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Propylparaben and Butylparaben — permitted, but with stricter limits in some markets&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style="line-height: 1.7; margin: 1em 0;"&gt;These two are still legal everywhere, but the EU and several other markets apply a stricter concentration cap.&lt;/p&gt;
